%% How one page render flows: server components first, client leaves last.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant N as Next.js (Vercel)
    participant P as app/ page (RSC)
    participant L as lib/ queries
    participant C as content/ modules
    participant I as Client island

    B->>N: GET /skills
    N->>P: render server component
    P->>L: queryEntries({ kind, craft, q })
    L->>C: read typed records
    C-->>L: RegistryEntry[]
    L-->>P: filtered + counted
    P-->>N: HTML + RSC payload
    N-->>B: streamed response (ISR cache hit: no render at all)
    B->>I: hydrate small client leaves
    I->>L: same query, in the client bundle
    L-->>I: RegistryEntry[]
    Note over I: search, filters, and the<br/>phone app run on real data,<br/>no API call needed
